From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PocketDS Linux Kit <pocketds-linux-kit@localhost>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: initialize property protocol
 unit

The SM8350-style property protocol exposes BATT_CHG_FULL_DESIGN and
BATT_CHG_FULL as charge properties.  Unlike the SC8280XP-style information
response, this protocol does not populate battmgr->unit.  Since the driver is
zero allocated, the unit otherwise remains QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mWh and both
charge properties always return -ENODATA.

Initialize the property-protocol variants to mAh.  The SC8280XP-style
variants continue to obtain their unit from BATTMGR_BAT_INFO.

Signed-off-by: PocketDS Linux Kit <pocketds-linux-kit@localhost>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 92a9729e93d5..88db4c507bd9 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1689,5 +1689,8 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_probe(struct auxiliary_device *adev,
 					     "failed to register wireless charing power supply\n");
 	} else {
+		/* The SM8350-style property protocol reports capacity as charge. */
+		battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh;
+
 		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550)
 			psy_desc = &sm8550_bat_psy_desc;
 		else
-- 
2.50.1
